<h2 id='what-is-cloudways'>🌐 What Is Cloudways?</h2>

<p>Cloudways is a managed cloud hosting platform that sits between you and the raw infrastructure of providers like DigitalOcean, AWS, Google Cloud, Linode (Akamai), and Vultr. Instead of spinning up a VPS yourself and spending days configuring Nginx, PHP-FPM, Redis, and SSL certificates, Cloudways handles the server layer while you focus on your website. You pick a cloud provider, pick a server size, and deploy your WordPress or PHP application in minutes.</p>

<p>For tour operators, that distinction matters. Most operators we work with are not running a dedicated IT department. The person managing the website is also quoting group tours, responding to booking inquiries, and building itineraries in <a href='https://traveloperator.io/reviews/rezdy-review'>Rezdy</a> or a similar booking platform. Managed hosting removes a category of work that most operators should not be doing themselves.</p>

<p>Cloudways was acquired by DigitalOcean in 2022 but continues to operate independently and still supports all five underlying cloud providers. The platform has matured significantly since that acquisition, with better uptime monitoring, a rebuilt dashboard, and the Cloudways CDN (powered by Cloudflare Enterprise) available as an add-on.</p>

<div class='callout-blue'>
  <strong>Tip:</strong> If you are currently on shared hosting with a provider like Bluehost or GoDaddy and your booking pages are loading in over 3 seconds, migrating to Cloudways on a DigitalOcean 2GB plan will typically cut that to under 1.5 seconds without any code changes. The Cloudways migration plugin handles the move with minimal downtime.
</div>

